<Layout title="Mårbacka" description="Nobel laureate Selma Lagerlöf's childhood home, a 20 minute drive from the farm.">
	<p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/activities">Activities</a> › <a href="/activities/culture-sights">Culture &amp; Sights</a> › Mårbacka</p>

	<div class="factcard">
		<div class="factcard-title">Mårbacka</div>
		<table>
			<tr><th>Type</th><td>Historic home &amp; museum</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Location</th><td>Östra Ämtervik</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Distance</th><td>~20 min drive</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Known for</th><td>Childhood home of Selma Lagerlöf</td></tr>
		</table>
	</div>

	<div class="page-header">
		<h1>Mårbacka</h1>
	</div>

	<div class="prose">
		<p>
			Mårbacka is the childhood home and estate of <strong>Selma Lagerlöf</strong>, the first
			woman to win the Nobel Prize in Literature (1909). She grew up here, later bought back the
			family estate as an adult, and rebuilt the manor house in the style you can visit today.
		</p>
		<p>
			The surrounding Fryksdalen valley — including <a href="/activities/rottneros-park">Rottneros
			Park</a>, just down the road — shows up thinly disguised throughout her fiction. See also
			the <a href="/history">history of Öjerviks gård</a>, which was itself the model for "Sjö"
			in her debut novel <em>Gösta Berlings saga</em>.
		</p>
	</div>
</Layout>
